  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: deaae056f5a3ccf4d8025ecf14452651, type: 3}
  m_Name: KARAMBIT_01
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: NusantaraAR.Runtime::NusantaraAR.ArtifactData
  artifactId: KARAMBIT_01
  displayName:
    id: Karambit Minangkabau
    en: Minangkabau Karambit
  localName: Kurambiak
  category: 0
  region:
    id: Minangkabau, Sumatra Barat
    en: Minangkabau, West Sumatra
  era:
    id: Tradisi Minangkabau; catatan tertulis tertua 1827
    en: Minangkabau tradition; earliest written record 1827
  summary:
    id: 'Kurambiak, pisau genggam kecil Minangkabau berbilah melengkung seperti cakar
      harimau, dengan lubang di ujung gagang untuk jari telunjuk. Model ini jenis
      jantan (7 gerigi di punggung bilah): hulu kayu kemuning berukir, cincin kuningan,
      dan sarung kayu berukir tinta emas. Model dibuat di Blender dari foto acuan
      dan data bersumber, bukan dipindai dari spesimen.'
    en: 'The kurambiak, a small Minangkabau hand-held knife whose blade curves like
      a tiger''s claw, with a ring at the end of the grip for the index finger. This
      model is the male type (7 serrations on the spine): a carved kemuning-wood
      hilt, a brass ferrule and a wooden sheath carved with gold-ink lines. It was
      made in Blender from reference photos and sourced data, not scanned from a
      specimen.'
  thumbnail: {fileID: 2800000, guid: 5833d5bbbaae03e42bdc68ff93fc6545, type: 3}
  prefab: {fileID: 545017950004828382, guid: 25c6c453a7237884da3c1609c14aaa46, type: 3}
  specimenOwner: 
  collectionNumber: 
  license: Model Blender milik proyek (dibuat dari foto acuan & data bersumber)
  measurementNote:
    id: "Skala 1:1 direka dari sumber: karambit 10,5 x 15,9 cm tanpa sarung, hulu
      \xB19,7 cm termasuk lubang (\xD8 dalam 2,2 cm), punggung bilah melengkung 120\xB0
      sepanjang 10,9 cm, tebal bilah 5 mm. Pembanding: karambit Met Museum 36.25.823ab
      14,6 cm. Bukan hasil pengukuran spesimen."
    en: "1:1 scale estimated from sources: the karambit is 10.5 x 15.9 cm without
      its sheath, the hilt ~9.7 cm including the ring (2.2 cm inner diameter), the
      spine curves 120\xB0 over 10.9 cm, the blade is 5 mm thick. For comparison,
      Met Museum karambit 36.25.823ab is 14.6 cm. Not measured from a specimen."
  markerCode: 50710
  isPlaceholder: 1
  placeholderNote:
    id: 'Model Blender dari foto acuan: ukiran, motif kaluak paku, dan serat kayu
      adalah penyederhanaan. Akan diganti aset dari spesimen asli yang divalidasi
      kurator.'
    en: 'Blender model from reference photos: the carving, kaluak paku motif and
      wood grain are simplified. It will be replaced by an asset from a curator-validated
      specimen.'
  hotspots:
  - hotspotId: lubang
    partName: Hulu
    localPosition: {x: -0.033199996, y: 0.09640001, z: -0.009277987}
    visibleFrom: 0
    title:
      id: Lubang
      en: Finger ring (lubang)
    regionalTerm: 'Minangkabau: lubang, lobang (lubang gagang)'
    material:
      id: 'Pada model: kayu kemuning, menyatu dengan hulu (perlu dikonfirmasi)'
      en: 'On the model: kemuning wood, one piece with the hilt (to be confirmed)'
    philosophy:
      id: '[Draf] Diisi kurator setelah spesimen asli ditetapkan.'
      en: '[Draft] To be written by the curator once the real specimen is chosen.'
    craft:
      id: Lubang di ujung atas gagang tempat jari telunjuk dimasukkan, sehingga lengkung
        bilah keluar dari bawah kepalan tangan. Ukurannya disesuaikan dengan jari
        pemiliknya. Karena jari terkait di lubang, karambit sulit dirampas lawan
        dan tidak mudah lepas dari genggaman.
      en: The ring at the top of the grip, where the index finger goes, so the curved
        blade emerges from the bottom of the fist. It is sized to its owner's finger.
        With the finger hooked through it, the karambit is hard to wrest away and
        does not slip from the grip.
    history:
      id: '[Draf] Diisi kurator setelah spesimen asli ditetapkan.'
      en: '[Draft] To be written by the curator once the real specimen is chosen.'
    narrationID: {fileID: 0}
    narrationEN: {fileID: 0}
    pronunciation: {fileID: 0}
    transcript:
      id: Lubang di ujung atas gagang tempat jari telunjuk dimasukkan, sehingga lengkung
        bilah keluar dari bawah kepalan tangan. Ukurannya disesuaikan dengan jari
        pemiliknya. Karena jari terkait di lubang, karambit sulit dirampas lawan
        dan tidak mudah lepas dari genggaman.
      en: The ring at the top of the grip, where the index finger goes, so the curved
        blade emerges from the bottom of the fist. It is sized to its owner's finger.
        With the finger hooked through it, the karambit is hard to wrest away and
        does not slip from the grip.
    sources:
    - 'Model: rekaan Blender dari foto acuan (Met 36.25.823ab, Kurambiak Minang -
      Wikimedia) & data bersumber'
    - 'Wiraseptya & Afdhal (2019) - Kajian Ikonografis Senjata Tradisional Kurambiak
      Minangkabau Cakar Harimau Sumatera, Majalah Ilmiah UPI YPTK 26(2): 100-108'
    - Wikipedia Indonesia - Kerambit (id.wikipedia.org/wiki/Kerambit)
    - Berita Minang (16-06-2025) - Mengenal Karambit, Senjata Rahasia Minangkabau
      yang Mendunia (beritaminang.com/berita/26346)
    curatorValidated: 0
    curatorNote: Diperiksa terhadap sumber daring (02-10-2026); menunggu validasi
      kurator.
  - hotspotId: hulu
    partName: Hulu
    localPosition: {x: -0.0034999996, y: 0.045, z: -0.011540699}
    visibleFrom: 0
    title:
      id: Hulu (Gagang)
      en: Hilt (hulu)
    regionalTerm: 'Minangkabau: gagang, hulu'
    material:
      id: 'Pada model: kayu kemuning berukir dengan pita hitam (perlu dikonfirmasi)'
      en: 'On the model: carved kemuning wood with black bands (to be confirmed)'
    philosophy:
      id: Kayu kemuning sering dipilih karena dipercaya bertuah. Sebagian pemilik
        mengukir gagangnya dengan motif-motif Minangkabau yang memuat falsafah adat.
      en: Kemuning wood is often chosen because it is believed to carry tuah (spiritual
        power). Some owners carve the grip with Minangkabau motifs that carry customary
        philosophy.
    craft:
      id: 'Gagang dibuat dari kayu, tanduk kerbau, atau gading. Menurut pedoman turun-temurun
        perajin di Sungai Pua (Agam), gagang idealnya selebar empat buku jari dan
        sepanjang tiga sampai empat ruas jari telunjuk, lalu disesuaikan dengan pemesan.
        Kurambiak Minang hanya berwarna di gagangnya, dan hanya dua warna: warna
        asli kayu dan hitam.'
      en: 'The grip is made of wood, water-buffalo horn or ivory. By a guideline
        handed down among the makers of Sungai Pua (Agam), it should ideally be four
        knuckles wide and three to four index-finger joints long, then adjusted to
        the customer. A Minang kurambiak is coloured only on its grip, and in just
        two colours: natural wood and black.'
    history:
      id: Dahulu permainan kurambiak hanya diwariskan kepada para datuk atau kalangan
        raja; tidak sembarang orang boleh menguasainya.
      en: In the past, the art of the kurambiak was passed down only to datuk (clan
        leaders) and royalty; not just anyone could master it.
    narrationID: {fileID: 0}
    narrationEN: {fileID: 0}
    pronunciation: {fileID: 0}
    transcript:
      id: 'Gagang dibuat dari kayu, tanduk kerbau, atau gading. Menurut pedoman turun-temurun
        perajin di Sungai Pua (Agam), gagang idealnya selebar empat buku jari dan
        sepanjang tiga sampai empat ruas jari telunjuk, lalu disesuaikan dengan pemesan.
        Kurambiak Minang hanya berwarna di gagangnya, dan hanya dua warna: warna
        asli kayu dan hitam.'
      en: 'The grip is made of wood, water-buffalo horn or ivory. By a guideline
        handed down among the makers of Sungai Pua (Agam), it should ideally be four
        knuckles wide and three to four index-finger joints long, then adjusted to
        the customer. A Minang kurambiak is coloured only on its grip, and in just
        two colours: natural wood and black.'
